#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD2257 expect=noViolation domain=TS
#note "All INDIC rows carry a valid dummy-SNOMED term in its preferred case (Headache, Nausea) - the flag-less rule compares case-sensitively per the D-TA-3 default (Fix #266). The blank-TSVAL INDIC row does not fire (completeness is another rule's concern) and the non-SNOMED value on the AGEMAX row is outside the INDIC condition."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#dictionaries dummy
dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col TSSEQ    type=Num
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
---
S01 | TS | 1 | INDIC  | Headache
S01 | TS | 2 | INDIC  | Nausea
S01 | TS | 3 | INDIC  |
S01 | TS | 4 | AGEMAX | NOTASNOMEDTERM
